;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljk:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; FOUR independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the British Crown, via Companies House
;;   * the National Stock Exchange of India, in its own published equity list
;;   * the issuer itself, at the website blueprint.edn records for it
;;
;; THE HOME REGISTER IS NOT AMONG THEM, AND THAT IS THE MAIN LIMITATION HERE.
;; GLEIF names RA000394 -- the Companies Register of India's Ministry of Corporate
;; Affairs -- as BOTH the register of record and the validation authority for this
;; entity (rows gleif-registered-at and gleif-validated-at). It could not be cited:
;; www.mca.gov.in answers HTTP 403. So the CIN L17110MH1973PLC019786, the single
;; most load-bearing identifier in this catalog, is attested by GLEIF ALONE. No row
;; below should be read as standing in for the Indian register.
;;
;; WHAT THE CORROBORATION ACTUALLY RUNS THROUGH. Two things, and they are different
;; in kind:
;;
;;   THE GROUP, through a state register that does answer. GLEIF says RELIANCE
;;   GLOBAL ENERGY SERVICES LIMITED, UK company 06626084, is a child of this LEI ->
;;   Companies House prints that name, that number and that registered office in its
;;   own record. Two authorities that never consulted each other agree on the
;;   subsidiary.
;;
;;   THE LISTED COMPANY, through an exchange. The NSE equity list names "Reliance
;;   Industries Limited", symbol RELIANCE, listed 29-NOV-1995, ISIN INE002A01018.
;;
;; NEITHER OF THOSE CARRIES THE CIN OR THE LEI. The UK register does not name the
;; parent at all -- row uk-ch-psc-none is the UK state affirmatively recording that
;; the subsidiary has NO person of significant control. NSE identifies by name and
;; domestic ISIN, and GLEIF does not carry INE002A01018 (its ISIN list holds only
;; the US-numbered GDR and bonds), so that row is new information rather than a
;; second witness to an existing one. The join from "the NSE-listed Reliance
;; Industries Limited" to "LEI 5493003UOETFYRONLG31" rests on the legal name.
;;
;; THE ISSUER DOES NAME ITSELF -- unlike some siblings in this catalog family. Both
;; cited ril.com pages carry "Reliance Industries Limited" in the <title>, and the
;; contact page publishes the Nariman Point address that GLEIF records. Those rows
;; are therefore :identity. The issuer does NOT publish its CIN on any page reached
;; here (checked: /privacy-policy, /contact-us, and the site root -- zero hits for
;; L17110MH1973PLC019786), so it corroborates the name and the address, not the
;; registration.
;;
;; :cite/row-kind is the honest part of this catalog and should be read before the
;; claims:
;;
;;   :identity   the substring names this entity, its identifiers, or a specific
;;               related legal entity. Point the URL at a different company and
;;               the row fails.
;;   :attribute  the substring is TRUE OF THIS ENTITY BUT NOT ONLY OF IT (status
;;               ACTIVE, country IN, city MUMBAI, legal form DDKQ). Such a row can
;;               survive a swap to a similar company. It is recorded because it is
;;               checked and true, not because it identifies.
;;   :definition the row resolves a code used by another row (RA000394, DDKQ), or
;;               fixes the column labels of a CSV. It says the named register or
;;               legal form exists; it says nothing about Reliance.
;;
;; Of the entries below, 29 are :identity, 21 are :attribute and 8 are
;; :definition. A reader who treats all 58 as identifying would overstate what this
;; catalog proves -- which is the error this field exists to prevent.
;;
;; Substrings are taken from the RAW response body and were each checked against
;; the fetched bytes before this file was written. Escaping facts found that way:
;;   * GLEIF escapes the forward slash, so gleif-ocid expects "in\\/L17110..." and
;;     gleif-ra-website expects "http:\\/\\/www.mca.gov.in\\/MCA21\\/"; the unescaped
;;     forms occur nowhere in the bytes.
;;
;; RELATIONSHIP ENDPOINTS ARE CITED SINGLY, NOT BY PAGE. GLEIF's /direct-children
;; is paginated and its page 1 is not a stable set, so a row against it would drift
;; for reasons that have nothing to do with this entity. Each related company is
;; instead cited through its OWN record plus its OWN /direct-parent (or
;; /ultimate-parent), which are single objects. Recron Malaysia has no direct-parent
;; record at all -- /direct-parent answers 404 -- so its row cites /ultimate-parent
;; and says so.
;;
;; SOURCES TESTED AND REJECTED. Each answered HTTP 2xx, which is exactly why they
;; are named here rather than silently dropped -- a row against any of them would
;; have passed forever and proved nothing. See :catalog/unreachable.


